#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199284} :activity/id #uuid "ea08cd43-7cea-59a6-a6eb-b25618d785bd" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048429 :topic/id #uuid "9eaae820-5193-5702-9ef4-efac567af4b5" :topic/math-academy-id 4136} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199284 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199466 :tutorial/content "Every division problem can be written as a fraction and vice-versa. In this lesson, we'll extend this idea to division problems involving negative numbers.\n\nTo begin, let's find a fraction that's equivalent to the following division problem:\n\n$$\n(-5) \\div 9\n$$\n\nNotice that we are dividing a negative number ${(\\color{red}{-5}})$ by a positive one $({\\color{blue}{9}})$. So the result will be negative:\n\n$$\nA\n$$\n\nTo write down the fraction that goes in the box, recall that\n\n$$\n5 \\div 9 = \\dfrac{5}{9}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}(-5)} \\div {\\color{blue}9} = {\\color{red}-\\dfrac{5}{9}}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "331c6a05-6da8-51c8-84ad-b69ff3dd9f56" :tutorial/math-academy-id 7635 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "77d5039f-8317-56ed-9c58-9503a2ff03cc" :step/math-academy-id 44285 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199285}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199285 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198381 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198023 :question/id #uuid "41696b59-d81e-5c49-a967-141f67934aa1" :question/math-academy-id "e-12359"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "65a25c72-9fa7-58fc-bf45-9cc2761696ea" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048624} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050719}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198587} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198588}] :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Division Problems as Fractions"} :step/id #uuid "04ca83ac-7a80-5eb8-8fb9-98dc863ddddb" :step/math-academy-id 44286 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199286}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199286 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198382 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198024 :question/id #uuid "e40e5f9e-aab7-53ed-8850-bd855f2b97a3" :question/math-academy-id "e-12360"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0fe851f3-482c-5426-87b2-32ec3c1b40f6" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048768}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198591} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198622}] :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Division Problems as Mixed Numbers"} :step/id #uuid "68dba314-3daa-559b-9888-94f883e881ef" :step/math-academy-id 44287 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199288}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199287 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198383 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198025 :question/id #uuid "a650b9e6-c97c-5471-af2d-76a5cfb0caff" :question/math-academy-id "e-12361"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d17ce34f-7d65-5f44-a1c0-dfd3c2ea55f6" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198589} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198590}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalent Fractions With Negative Numbers"} :step/id #uuid "af22cc6e-47b4-5a18-a2b1-50d51596813e" :step/math-academy-id 44288} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199288 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199467 :tutorial/content "What is the missing part of the expression below?\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{41}{8} = \\dfrac{\\bbox[1pt, border: 1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}}{-8}\n$$\n\nA negative number can be obtained if we divide two numbers, one of which is positive and the other negative.\n\nSo, given a negative fraction, we have the following equivalent notations:\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{41}{8} = \\dfrac{-41}{8} = \\dfrac{41}{-8}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we see that the denominator on the right-hand side is negative $({{\\color{red}-8}})$. Therefore, the missing numerator must be $({{\\color{blue}41}}){:}$\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{41}{8} = \\dfrac{\\bbox[2pt, border: 1pt solid black]{\\color{blue}41}}{-8}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "652d8025-fc3e-56b0-ac6a-10bc44ecaf15" :tutorial/math-academy-id 7636 :tutorial/title "Equivalent Fractions With Negative Numbers"} :step/id #uuid "c1d49b55-ca98-5e16-a9de-14e2aaf4fe80" :step/math-academy-id 44289 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199287}}] :activity/title "Equivalent Fractions With Negative Numbers" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186198482}]}
